  "capturedAt": "2026-11-02T20:11:38.182Z",
  "markdown": "![EMPTY ALT](/logo.jpg)\n\n[link] [Afyawise](/)\n\n[link] [Home](/)\n\n[link] [Blog](/blog)\n\n[link] [Shop](/shop)\n\n[link] [Support Us](/support)\n\n[link] [About us](/about)\n\n[link] [Our Work](/work)\n\n[link] [Services](/services)\n\n[link] [Our Impact](/our-impact)\n\n[link] [Our Team](/team)\n\n[link] [Contact Us](/contact)\n\n### WHO WE ARE\n\nAfyaWise Community Based Organization is a grassroots initiative in Meru County empowering healthier communities through local solutions. We focus on maternal and child health, mental health, wellness, Persons Living with Disability and WASH (water, sanitation, and hygiene). Guided by five core goals, AfyaWise expands access to care, builds community capacity, and promotes lasting health practices across Meru and beyond.\n\n![EMPTY ALT](/assets/who-we-are-D-xmnnKN.jpg)\n\n![EMPTY ALT](/assets/vision-DvZuxefr.png)\n\n### OUR VISION\n\nA healthy and informed society empowered to support County s sustainable Health Coverage.\n\n### OUR MISSION\n\nTo enhance health literacy, advocate for equitable healthcare access, and implement sustainable health solutions within communities.\n\n![EMPTY ALT](/assets/mission-DGOqaG8U.png)\n\n![EMPTY ALT](/assets/core-values-B6tNLccU.png)\n\n## Our Core Values\n\n- Inclusivity: Embracing diversity and ensuring no one is left behind\n\n- Transparency:Operating with openness and accountability\n\n- Community-Centered:Prioritizing the needs of the community in all activities\n\n- Sustainability:Promoting lasting solutions to healthcare challenges\n\n- Collaboration:Building partnerships with stakeholders to maximize impact.\n\n## Our Objectives\n\n- To increase access to quality prenatal, antenatal, and postnatal care services for women of reproductive age in target communities by 40% within two years.\n\n- To reduce the prevalence of common childhood illnesses (e.g., diarrhea, pneumonia, and malnutrition) by 30% through community-based nutrition and immunization programs within 24 months.\n\n- To establish and support at least five community-based mental health support groups and referral systems for early diagnosis and treatment within one year.\n\n- To increase the percentage of households practicing safe water handling, proper sanitation, and handwashing with soap by 50% in the project areas within 18 months.\n\n- To train 100 community health volunteers (CHVs) and local leaders on integrated health promotion strategies for maternal, child, mental health, and WASH by the end of the first project year.\n\n## Our Programs & Activities\n\n- Maternal & Child Health Programs\n\n- Mental Health and Disability Inclusion\n\n- Community Wellness Initiatives\n\n- Health Education & Awareness\n\n- Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH)\n\n- Partnerships & Resource Mobilization\n\n- Environmental Health Advocacy\n\n![EMPTY ALT](/assets/programs_activities-BhLioFBt.jpg)\n\n![EMPTY ALT](/assets/impact-B-jiAYnh.png)\n\n## OUR IMPACT\n\nSince its inception, AfyaWise has improved health literacy, expanded healthcare access, and empowered hundreds of community members across Meru County. Through strategic partnerships and committed local leadership, AfyaWise continues building healthy communities one step at a time.\n\n[button] Chat with us\n\n![Chat Icon](/agent.jpg)\n\n![Afyawise logo](/logo.jpg)\n\n# Afyawise\n\nPromoting community health and well-being\n\n## Quick Links\n\n- Home  _(links: Home -> /)_\n\n- About  _(links: About -> /about)_\n\n- Our Team  _(links: Our Team -> /team)_\n\n- Our Work  _(links: Our Work -> /work)_\n\n### CONTACT\n\n![Email](Icons/email-white.svg)\n\n[link] [info@afyawise.org](mailto:info@afyawise.org)\n\n![Phone](Icons/phone-color.svg)\n\n[link] [+254798724766](tel:+254798724766)\n\n![Location](Icons/location-color.svg)\n\nKarama Ward, Meru County, Kenya\n\n© 2025 AfyaWise CBO. All rights reserved.",
  "innerText": "Afyawise\nHome\nBlog\nShop\nSupport Us\nAbout us\nOur Work\nServices\nOur Impact\nOur Team\nContact Us\nWHO WE ARE\n\nAfyaWise Community Based Organization is a grassroots initiative in Meru County empowering healthier communities through local solutions. We focus on maternal and child health, mental health, wellness, Persons Living with Disability and WASH (water, sanitation, and hygiene). Guided by five core goals, AfyaWise expands access to care, builds community capacity, and promotes lasting health practices across Meru and beyond.\n\nOUR VISION\n\nA healthy and informed society empowered to support County s sustainable Health Coverage.\n\nOUR MISSION\n\nTo enhance health literacy, advocate for equitable healthcare access, and implement sustainable health solutions within communities.\n\nOur Core Values\nInclusivity: Embracing diversity and ensuring no one is left behind\nTransparency:Operating with openness and accountability\nCommunity-Centered:Prioritizing the needs of the community in all activities\nSustainability:Promoting lasting solutions to healthcare challenges\nCollaboration:Building partnerships with stakeholders to maximize impact.\nOur Objectives\nTo increase access to quality prenatal, antenatal, and postnatal care services for women of reproductive age in target communities by 40% within two years.\nTo reduce the prevalence of common childhood illnesses (e.g., diarrhea, pneumonia, and malnutrition) by 30% through community-based nutrition and immunization programs within 24 months.\nTo establish and support at least five community-based mental health support groups and referral systems for early diagnosis and treatment within one year.\nTo increase the percentage of households practicing safe water handling, proper sanitation, and handwashing with soap by 50% in the project areas within 18 months.\nTo train 100 community health volunteers (CHVs) and local leaders on integrated health promotion strategies for maternal, child, mental health, and WASH by the end of the first project year.\nOur Programs & Activities\nMaternal & Child Health Programs\nMental Health and Disability Inclusion\nCommunity Wellness Initiatives\nHealth Education & Awareness\nWater, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH)\nPartnerships & Resource Mobilization\nEnvironmental Health Advocacy\nOUR IMPACT\n\nSince its inception, AfyaWise has improved health literacy, expanded healthcare access, and empowered hundreds of community members across Meru County. Through strategic partnerships and committed local leadership, AfyaWise continues building healthy communities one step at a time.\n\nAfyawise\n\nPromoting community health and well-being\n\nQuick Links\nHome\nAbout\nOur Team\nOur Work\nCONTACT\ninfo@afyawise.org\n+254798724766\nKarama Ward, Meru County, Kenya\n\n© 2025 AfyaWise CBO.\nAll rights reserved.",
